        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/satsuma/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s historic Old Satsuma School, now the public library, earned a spot on the Alabama Register of Landmarks and Heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/satsuma/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Satsuma celebrated its 50th anniversary of incorporation in 2009, marking a half-century of community resilience rooted in agriculture.",
